      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism in constitutional interpretation generally argues that the Constitution should be understood based on the meaning it had at the time of its adoption or ratification. Proponents argue this limits judicial subjectivity, ensuring the law reflects the public understanding of the framers, rather than the judge's modern policy preferences. The main legal justification is that the Constitution is a fixed, foundational document, not a living one that can be constantly reinterpreted to suit current social needs.",
