      "content": "i get the theoretical side of it, but doesn't that approach basically ignore how much society has changed? if we just stick to what people thought in the 1700s, it seems like it's impossible to handle modern rights or tech issues. wouldn't a \"living constitution\" approach be more legitimate and practical for a modern democracy than trying to be a historian?",
