      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"living constitution\" approach directly addresses this by arguing that the Constitution's broad principles are designed to *adapt* to evolving real-world circumstances. Proponents of the living constitution suggest that the structure and language inherently allow for contemporary interpretation to make the document relevant to modern society and technology. They view the rigid application of 18th-century understanding as a threat to democratic progress and the effective protection of rights in a rapidly changing world.",
      "source": "target",
